4.
Particulars to be included in the notice.
- The notice shall state-
(i)
the name of the coupe or the mahal;
(ii)
the particulars necessary for its identification ;
(iii)
the period for which it is proposed to be settled ;
(iv)
the last date and time for submission of tender;
(v)
the officer to whom and the manner in which the tender is to be submitted ;
(vi)
the place at which the tender is to be submitted ;
(vii)
the earnest money that will have to be paid ;
(viii)
in the case of Royalty-cum-Monopoly Sale, the minimum stipulated quantity should be quoted ;
(ix)
any other particulars deemed necessary by the authority calling for tender.
